  "why": "draft/<league>/choices serves a league's current or next draft, not a history. Dunelmliga re-drafts at GW21, so the API returned an empty choices list for the GW1 draft from the moment that second draft was scheduled. Without this file every player in the league reads as Not Originally Drafted.",
  "source": "Captured live during the draft by the private draft-night tooling, which recorded element id, drafter short_name and 0-based overall pick order.",
  "derived": "index = n + 1. pick and round are computed from index and the six drafters, matching how the API numbers a snake draft (verified against league 19116). entry is the entry_id looked up from the league details by short_name.",
  "not_captured": "choice_time and seconds_to_pick. Nothing downstream reads them.",
  "verified": "89 of the 90 picks were still held by the drafter who made them at GW1; the exception (element 239, MN) is an explicit free-agent move in the transfers table."
